server : a slot file carries the LoRA config its state was computed with

Since upstream #32434 (b12498) a slot's prompt carries the LoRA config its tokens were processed
with (server_prompt::lora): launch_slot_with_task() compares a task's adapters with it, the
host-memory prompt cache stores it with every state and skips the states of another config. A slot
file does not store it (upstream's TODO in server-slot-sched.h), and SLOT_RESTORE leaves
prompt.lora as it was -- empty in a never-used slot. On a server started with --lora the first
task then read the restored state as "computed under no adapters" and cleared it (F240: 77 of 79
prompt tokens evaluated again), and in a slot that had served a task under other adapters the
restored state kept that slot's label.

The patch appends the config to the slot file, after the checkpoints and the draft state, as a
section of its own ("SLRA", version 1: per adapter its path and its scale), and a restore labels the
state with it on the adapters loaded at that time, matched by path; an adapter the section does not
name has scale 0. A state computed under no adapters writes no section, and a file without one --
upstream's format, or one saved by a server without adapters -- counts as computed under none, which
is what upstream assumes for a never-used slot: the first task with adapters clears it. A section
that cannot be read, data after the state that no section reads (a checkpoint or draft section that
could not be read -- cut, or of another version -- behind which the config may lie), or a section
that names an adapter at a scale other than 0 which this server has not loaded, refuses the restore
(invalid request) and leaves the slot empty: no task of this server computes under that config, and
"none" for an unknown config would reuse a state computed with adapters on a server without any.
Upstream's reader ignores what follows its sections, so upstream reads these files as before. Not
reset by a refused restore: the speculative state a draft section set, as upstream's SLOT_ERASE
leaves it too.

Only the scales and paths are stored, never the adapter infos: a wake from the idle sleep frees the
adapters and loads them again, and a stored info would carry a pointer into freed memory
(are_lora_equal compares the pointers, lora_should_clear_cache reads through them).

History: until the review of 2026-11-19 the patch kept the scales of every file the server saved in
a map by path, so a file of an earlier process, or a copy under another name, counted as computed
under none; in the first round of the review of 2026-11-18 it stored the adapter infos themselves
(pointers that a sleep frees); before it, it labelled a restored state with the server's adapters at
the time of the restore, which reused a state saved under scale 1 after setLoraAdapters() had set
scale 0; until b12497 it started every slot with slot.lora = params_base.lora_adapters in init(),
which upstream's comparison no longer reads.

The guard is src/test/cpp/test_lora_cache.cpp: its LoraCacheFreshSlot fixture restores slot 0's
saved state into the never-used slot 1, which must reuse it; restores a state saved under other
scales, which may not be reused, and a copy of a file under another name, which may; and refuses a
truncated section. LoraCacheFiles restores a file into a model loaded again, which must reuse it,
refuses it in a model without the adapter, restores a file saved without adapters, which the first
task clears, and refuses a file whose draft section was cut (the section behind it lost);
LoraCacheSleep restores a state after the model slept, which must be reused. The other cases hold
upstream's half.

Drop-check on every bump: read the SLOT_SAVE and SLOT_RESTORE cases in
tools/server/server-context.cpp at the new tag -- once the slot file stores the LoRA config and the
restore sets prompt.lora from it, drop the patch; if upstream stores it in another form, a file
written by this patch is still read by upstream (it ignores the trailing section).

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -2963,6 +2963,103 @@ private:
         return n_read;
     }
 
+    // the LoRA config the state was computed with follows the draft state: the llama state payload
+    // does not carry it (server_prompt::lora, the TODO in server-slot-sched.h), and the next task and
+    // the prompt cache compare a restored state with it. One entry per adapter of the config: the
+    // adapter's path and its scale.
+    static constexpr uint32_t SLOT_LORA_MAGIC   = 0x41524c53; // "SLRA"
+    static constexpr uint32_t SLOT_LORA_VERSION = 1;
+
+    // returns false if the config could not be written completely; a state computed under no
+    // adapters writes nothing, which a restore reads as none
+    bool save_slot_lora(const std::string & filepath, const server_slot & slot, size_t & n_written) const {
+        n_written = 0;
+        if (slot.prompt.lora.empty()) {
+            return true;
+        }
+        std::ofstream ofs(std::filesystem::u8path(filepath), std::ios::binary | std::ios::app);
+        if (!ofs) {
+            SLT_WRN(slot, "failed to append the LoRA config to '%s'\n", filepath.c_str());
+            return false;
+        }
+        const uint32_t magic   = SLOT_LORA_MAGIC;
+        const uint32_t version = SLOT_LORA_VERSION;
+        const uint32_t count   = (uint32_t) slot.prompt.lora.size();
+        ckpt_write(ofs, &magic,   sizeof(magic),   n_written);
+        ckpt_write(ofs, &version, sizeof(version), n_written);
+        ckpt_write(ofs, &count,   sizeof(count),   n_written);
+        for (const auto & lora : slot.prompt.lora) {
+            ckpt_write_buf(ofs, lora.path, n_written);
+            ckpt_write(ofs, &lora.scale, sizeof(lora.scale), n_written);
+        }
+        ofs.flush();
+        if (!ofs) {
+            SLT_WRN(slot, "failed to append the LoRA config to '%s' - the config is incomplete\n", filepath.c_str());
+            return false;
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    // sets the restored state's config on the adapters loaded now, by path (a wake from the idle sleep
+    // loads them again, under new pointers; an adapter the file does not name has scale 0) and returns
+    // the bytes consumed. A file without the section counts as computed under no adapters, as upstream
+    // assumes for a never-used slot. Throws when the section cannot be read or cannot be found behind
+    // the other sections, or names an adapter at a scale other than 0 that this server has not loaded:
+    // no task here computes under that config.
+    size_t load_slot_lora(const std::string & filepath, size_t offset, server_slot & slot) const {
+        slot.prompt.lora.clear();
+        std::ifstream ifs(std::filesystem::u8path(filepath), std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);
+        const size_t file_size = ifs ? (size_t) ifs.tellg() : 0;
+        if (!ifs || file_size < offset || !ifs.seekg(offset)) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        const size_t n_avail = file_size - offset;
+        if (n_avail == 0) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        size_t n_read = 0;
+        uint32_t magic   = 0;
+        uint32_t version = 0;
+        uint32_t count   = 0;
+        // bytes that neither the checkpoints nor the draft state read: one of those sections could not
+        // be read (cut, or of another version), and this section, behind it, cannot be found
+        if (!ckpt_read(ifs, &magic, sizeof(magic), n_read) || magic != SLOT_LORA_MAGIC) {
+            throw std::runtime_error("the slot save file holds data after its state that cannot be read (a damaged "
+                                     "context checkpoint or draft section), so its LoRA config is unknown");
+        }
+        if (!ckpt_read(ifs, &version, sizeof(version), n_read) || version != SLOT_LORA_VERSION ||
+            !ckpt_read(ifs, &count,   sizeof(count),   n_read)) {
+            throw std::runtime_error("invalid LoRA config in the slot save file");
+        }
+        std::vector<common_adapter_lora_info> lora = params_base.lora_adapters;
+        for (auto & adapter : lora) {
+            adapter.scale = 0.0f;
+        }
+        std::vector<bool> named(lora.size(), false);
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
+            std::string path;
+            float scale = 0.0f;
+            if (!ckpt_read_buf(ifs, path, n_avail, n_read) || !ckpt_read(ifs, &scale, sizeof(scale), n_read)) {
+                throw std::runtime_error("truncated LoRA config in the slot save file");
+            }
+            size_t j = 0;
+            while (j < lora.size() && (named[j] || lora[j].path != path)) {
+                ++j;
+            }
+            if (j == lora.size()) {
+                if (scale != 0.0f) {
+                    throw std::runtime_error("the state was computed with the LoRA adapter '" + path + "' at scale " +
+                                             std::to_string(scale) + ", which this server has not loaded");
+                }
+                continue;
+            }
+            named[j] = true;
+            lora[j].scale = scale;
+        }
+        slot.prompt.lora = std::move(lora);
+        return n_read;
+    }
+
     // returns false to decline the task, it is offered again after the decode is done
     bool process_single_task(server_task && task, bool is_yielding) {
         // while yielding, an encode / decode is running and only reading the server state is safe
@@ -3237,6 +3334,12 @@ private:
                         break;
                     }
 
+                    size_t nwrite_lora = 0;
+                    if (!save_slot_lora(filepath, *slot, nwrite_lora)) {
+                        send_error(task, "Unable to save slot: incomplete LoRA config", ERROR_TYPE_SERVER);
+                        break;
+                    }
+
                     const int64_t t_end = ggml_time_us();
                     const double t_save_ms = (t_end - t_start) / 1000.0;
 
@@ -3246,7 +3349,7 @@ private:
                     res->filename = filename;
                     res->is_save  = true;
                     res->n_tokens = slot->prompt.tokens.size();
-                    res->n_bytes  = nwrite + nwrite_ckpt + nwrite_dft;
+                    res->n_bytes  = nwrite + nwrite_ckpt + nwrite_dft + nwrite_lora;
                     res->t_ms     = t_save_ms;
                     queue_results.send(std::move(res));
                 } break;
@@ -3306,6 +3409,15 @@ private:
                     const size_t nread_ckpt = load_slot_checkpoints(filepath, nread, *slot);
                     const size_t nread_dft  = load_slot_draft(filepath, nread + nread_ckpt, *slot);
 
+                    size_t nread_lora = 0;
+                    try {
+                        nread_lora = load_slot_lora(filepath, nread + nread_ckpt + nread_dft, *slot);
+                    } catch (const std::exception & err) {
+                        slot->prompt_clear();
+                        send_error(task, std::string("Unable to restore slot: ") + err.what(), ERROR_TYPE_INVALID_REQUEST);
+                        break;
+                    }
+
                     const int64_t t_end = ggml_time_us();
                     const double t_restore_ms = (t_end - t_start) / 1000.0;
 
@@ -3315,7 +3427,7 @@ private:
                     res->filename = filename;
                     res->is_save  = false;
                     res->n_tokens = slot->prompt.tokens.size();
-                    res->n_bytes  = nread + nread_ckpt + nread_dft;
+                    res->n_bytes  = nread + nread_ckpt + nread_dft + nread_lora;
                     res->t_ms     = t_restore_ms;
                     queue_results.send(std::move(res));
                 } break;
